    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d638">

                <pb facs="0632" n="620" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg620"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/852: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-01-18T18:00:00+09:00">January 18, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 18—9:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8. Department’s 9, January 16, 5 p.m. Clive made oral and written representations
                    today as outlined in Department’s telegram. Arita<anchor n="8" xml:id="d638-f1"
                    /> replied that the Japanese Navy is opposed to accepting a qualitative without
                    a quantitative limit but that he would investigate and would <pb facs="0633"
                        n="621" xml:id="pg621"/> try to give a reply “in a week or a little more”.
                    Clive pressed him for a more urgent reply. He has promised to inform me as soon
                    as the reply is received.</p>
                <p>Clive says that both the British and German Naval Attachés believe that the
                    Japanese naval authorities are now considering the construction of battleships
                    of 50,000 tons with 18-inch guns.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d638-f1" n="8" xml:id="d638-f1-content">
                <p>K. Arita, Japanese Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
